      "writtenOn": "2026-02-04T07:08:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is this ok?  kernfs works for many filesystems at once (configfs, sysfs, cgroups, etc.), so would this overwrite an event for a different filesystem?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1476,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1476,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "56a2551d7125e2c12d7ff3db63d079662a55e425",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f542d17_f67aa6ca",
        "filename": "fs/kernfs/dir.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1476,
      "author": {
        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T17:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure how that would happen. Shouldn\u0027t each of those filesystems have a different set of `kernfs_node`s for their distinct hierarchies of dirs/files?\n\nThis does mean a modify event doesn\u0027t get sent if the file gets deleted before the workqueue processes the `kernfs_node` in question... but I think that\u0027s reasonable because the file can\u0027t be read after its deleted, so I\u0027m not sure what use there would be for receiving a `MODIFY` event in that case.\n\nTo send out both a `MODIFY` and a `DELETE` event right after would require changing the `kernfs_notify_list` design so that multiple events can be queued for the same `kernfs_node`, which is not currently possible because `kernfs_elem_attr`\u0027s `notify_next` can only have one spot on the `kernfs_notify_list`. Or maybe we could multiplex multiple events in the same `notify_event` field and deal with sending the multiple events in `kernfs_notify_workfn`, but that might end up as a complicated mess.",
      "parentUuid": "81f7d516_cc20de1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1476,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1476,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "56a2551d7125e2c12d7ff3db63d079662a55e425",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c520c07_d769d689",
        "filename": "fs/kernfs/dir.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1476,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T12:14:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, yes, you are right, they will have a different set of nodes.  I got tripped up by the \"global\" lock being used here in thinking that this was just one list.\n\nAnd yes, I think that the lack of a modify if a delete happens before it gets sent out should be ok, but I do not know what userspace is expecting to have happen.  What happens on a \"normal\" filesystem in this case?",
      "parentUuid": "4f542d17_f67aa6ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1476,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1476,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "56a2551d7125e2c12d7ff3db63d079662a55e425",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
