        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-08T01:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`fsnotify` queues all events independently so this doesn\u0027t look like an issue for normal filesystems that perform the fsnotify calls synchronously. (grep for `fsnotify_modify`)\n\nHowever normal files are still readable after they are removed/unlinked as long as there\u0027s still an open file descriptor, but kernfs files are not.",
      "parentUuid": "2c520c07_d769d689",
      "range": {
