        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T17:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Originally either `fsnotify` or `fsnotify_inode` was called, depending on if the parent inode could be found. `fsnotify` handles sending `MODIFY` events to both a watched file and its parent. So a single call to `fsnotify` works for `MOIDFY`, and the `fsnotify_inode` call can be skipped.\n\n`fsnotify` does **not** handle sending both a `DELETE` event to the parent and a `DELETE_SELF` event to the watched file. Given `FS_DELETE` `fsnotify` only sends a `DELETE` event to the parent. So the `fsnotify_inode` call cannot be skipped in the case where the watched node is deleted, and we have to convert the event into a `_SELF` version for that call. The `self_event !\u003d notify_event` check detects this case.\n\nCome to think of it, I should probably also try adding `FS_IN_IGNORED` in this case so the watch gets automatically removed by inotify without having to call `inotify_rm_watch` in userspace.",
      "parentUuid": "a151f655_18e5e061",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 978,
        "startChar": 19,
